# A known bug that nobody reproduced upstream (../../RESULTS.md, finding 5; Meilisearch issues
# #4584 and #6202, closed). Build ../hydo.yaml. The kill keeps Meilisearch
# down during steps 0 and 1, step 1 removes its database, and the restart before step 2 creates a
# new one, whose VERSION file Meilisearch writes through a temporary file and a rename without a
# sync. Step 3 enqueues a document addition, and the power goes off right after its 202. The
# recovery boot's Meilisearch stops at every start with "failed to infer the version of the
# database": VERSION is empty or missing in a database that is not empty. The run ends with
# "VIOLATION service cannot recover (committed data unrecoverable) (meilisearch)", fingerprint
# 3a1aec7c61e5c7fc on hvx with the image 999ebd681046eb44. With --set fresh=no (the database
# kept, VERSION written again over the old file) the schedule passes.
#   hydo run <image> "$(tail -1 new-database-unstartable-after-power-cut.schedule)"
# expect: violation      (change to ok when the bug is fixed)
disk=cut | run K=meilisearch@0+2 C=4
